Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 17:27:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 031/154] test: the visible-tab command set had no test and
 decays silently
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 2's routing was already implemented - every command the task enumerates
is in CommandTarget, the bubble anchor already resolves the presenter
separately, and CreateWindowSlot already seeds from the visible profile. The
task stayed open while the work sat in the tree.

What was genuinely missing is a way to know that stays true. The set lived
inside AtriumNativeWidgetMac::CommandTarget, wrapped around a Browser* and a
views:: widget, so nothing could reach it. It is the kind of list that rots
without failing: drop a command and it acts on an OFF-SCREEN tab, which the
user experiences as the menu item doing nothing at all. Zoom did exactly that
before stage 2.

The set moves into atrium_command_target_decision.h as a command id in and a
bool out, the same posture as the routing and peek decisions. CommandTarget
keeps only the job of resolving that answer against live objects.

Five tests, split by the stage that introduced each group so a regression names
where it broke. Two are about what must NOT be in the set: app-scoped commands
stay on the invoking window, and IDC_NEW_WINDOW is called out by name because
it reads like an omission and is not - it resolves the visible PROFILE inside
CreateWindowSlot, and adding it here would double-resolve it. An unknown
command has its own case so a future range check cannot sweep the set wider
than intended.

Checked they can fail rather than assuming: removing IDC_BOOKMARK_THIS_TAB
turns the stage-2 case red and nothing else, which is the granularity the split
was for.

No behaviour change.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
